## Retry / Backoff

**Rule:** retry `5xx` and connectivity failures only. **Never retry 4xx** — the client must fix
the request. Retrying 4xx amplifies load without any chance of success.

| Parameter | Value | Notes |
|-----------|-------|-------|
| Max attempts | 3 | Includes the initial attempt |
| Initial interval | 1 s | |
| Max interval | 30 s | Cap prevents unbounded wait |
| Multiplier | 2× | Exponential backoff |
| Jitter | 50 % | Prevents thundering-herd on simultaneous failures |
| Retryable | `5xx`, `ConnectException`, `SocketTimeoutException` | |
| Non-retryable | `4xx` | Surface immediately; do not retry |

---

## Timeout Budget

**5 s per attempt** — not for the whole retry sequence. Total worst-case: `5 s × 3 = 15 s`,
plus backoff between retries (`1 s + 2 s = 3 s`), so ≈18 s maximum. Set your caller's timeout
to accommodate this if the call is synchronous and user-facing.

