## Rate Limiter

Token-bucket defaults: **100 req/s sustained, burst 20, keyed per client/tenant**.

Apply upstream (at the entry point, not the outbound adapter) to protect your service from
overload. If you are calling a third-party API, apply the rate limiter at the outbound adapter
keyed on the external service to stay within their quota.

<% if (language === 'typescript' || language === 'multi') { %>
```typescript
import { RateLimiterMemory } from 'rate-limiter-flexible'

const rateLimiter = new RateLimiterMemory({
  points: 100,     // 100 tokens
  duration: 1,     // per second
})

// Burst: allow 20 extra
const burstLimiter = new RateLimiterMemory({
  points: 20,
  duration: 1,
  blockDuration: 0,
})
```
