## External-call / Adapter Checklist

When adding a new external call or adapter, verify each item:

- [ ] **Isolated CB+retry instance per target** — one per external service/tenant, lazily created
      and cached by key. Shared instances amplify blast radius across unrelated targets.
- [ ] **Config at instance creation** — values read once at construction time. Explicit cache
      invalidation (restart or reload) required to pick up changes.
- [ ] **Test seam** — inject a configurable interval/delay function so integration tests can
      use fast (0 ms) intervals without touching production configuration.
- [ ] **Graceful degradation** — invalid or missing config falls back to the defaults above,
      not to an error or panic.
- [ ] **SSRF allowlist** — validate outbound URLs at dispatch time: require HTTPS, block
      private RFC-1918 ranges, loopback (127.x, ::1), and link-local (169.254.x).
- [ ] **No secrets in logs** — sanitize URLs (strip query tokens), headers, and response bodies
      before logging. Never log Authorization or X-Api-Key values.
- [ ] **At-least-once delivery** — retry semantics mean consumers must be idempotent. Document
      this contract in the consumer's integration guide.
- [ ] **Dead-letter after max attempts** — route undeliverable messages to a DLQ or dead-letter
      topic after exhausting retries. Do not silently drop.
- [ ] **Retry on 5xx only** — verify the retry predicate excludes 4xx explicitly. A broad
      `catch(Exception)` retry predicate is a bug.

